GMAT Py DE405 selected-body SPK
================================

Modified kernel producer / last modifier: GMAT Py maintainers.
Institution: GMAT Py independent open-source project.
Modification date: 2026-10-01.
Generated by the GMAT Py rebuild_ephemeris.c utility with CSPICE N0067 SPKSUB.
This file was produced by GMAT Py; it is not an original JPL/NAIF kernel.

Scientific origin and reproducible input lineage (not current producer):
Original data were developed by NASA/JPL Solar System Dynamics and
provided as SPICE kernels by NASA/JPL NAIF.
Inputs: DE405, JUP230, SAT132, URA063, NEP057, and PLU006.
Standish, E.M. (1998), JPL Planetary and Lunar Ephemerides DE405/LE405,
JPL IOM 312.F-98-048.

Method: copy original Chebyshev segments using SPKSUB, retaining target,
center, J2000 frame, type and start/end ET bounds from the GMAT
DE405AllPlanets.bsp template. No samples were refitted or interpolated.
The template supplies only selection descriptors; all astronomical
coefficient payloads come directly from the authoritative input kernels.
Exact coverage by target (seconds TDB past J2000) is recorded below.

Redistribution basis: https://naif.jpl.nasa.gov/naif/rules.html
Changed filename and producer metadata identify this modified kernel.
Original source producer information above describes scientific lineage.
Validation: 20 segment descriptors/ranges preserved; 860 deterministic
position/velocity comparisons against the original GMAT kernel gave
exact equality (zero position and velocity differences).

